module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- kinds.fenel — well-kindedness predicates over a marshalled KindType.
-- unified-static-analysis Phase 5a (brief:
--   workstreams/unified-static-analysis/briefs/phase-5a-kind-predicates-isunaryconstructor.md).
--
-- THE GAP THIS CLOSES. Fenel ships Functor / Monad / Monoid as live
-- constructor-polymorphic classes (algebra.fenel / algebra-instances.fenel),
-- dispatched via the universal {$el:{call}} matcher — but there is NO
-- well-kindedness CHECKER: nothing rejects `Functor Int` (a nullary type where
-- a unary constructor is required). D-C's dispatch mechanism already SHIPS
-- (match-structural.fenel: matchStructural / checkPredicateBound(s) + the
-- worked `isRecordType : TraversalType -> Bool` template). This file is the
-- AUTHORING slice (5a): the kind-ARITY predicates (`*`, `* -> *`, `* -> * -> *`)
-- modelled byte-for-byte on isRecordType, ADVISORY + unit-tested. The resolver
-- wire (5b) + the ByPattern registration (5c) are the SUCCESSOR slices; this
-- slice touches NO resolver, kernel, totality, or class decl.
--
-- THE CRUX (why a seam, the 3b-6 return-table precedent). isRecordType is
-- purely STRUCTURAL — TtRecord is recognisable from the marshalled shape alone.
-- "is `Maybe` a unary constructor?" is NOT: it is a question about Maybe's
-- declared type-param ARITY (`Maybe a` ⇒ 1 ⇒ kind `* -> *`), a REGISTRY fact a
-- `.fenel` body cannot reach. So the constructor's arity is surfaced at the
-- kind-marshal seam (marshalKindType, engine-bodies-dispatch.ts — category B,
-- the EXACT 3b-6 return-table precedent: a registry READ, not language logic),
-- and the predicate reads it STRUCTURALLY off the marshalled KindType.
--
-- THE `$`-KEY BARRIER + NO ENTITY DECLS (the type-to-set.fenel / propagate.fenel
-- audit-green invariant). A `.fenel` body cannot author/read `$`-prefixed-key
-- objects, so the marshalled KindType is a PLAIN record dispatched by a `tag`
-- STRING field (NOT `$tag`, NOT a registered ADT) — the exact TypeMarker /
-- SetMarker discipline. Entity + law count move +0.
--
-- KindType (TS-built by marshalKindType, dispatched by the `tag` field — the
-- 4-arm minimal mirror, only the arms the predicates read; D-5a-3 settled on a
-- minimal PARALLEL marker, NOT an `arity` field on TraversalType, so the hot
-- marshalTraversalType path + its ~20 structural-dispatch consumers stay
-- byte-identical — zero oracle risk — and the registry read happens ONLY when
-- kind-checking):
--   { tag = "KtCon", name = String, arity = Number } — a named type constructor
--       + its declared type-param arity (0 = nullary/proper, 1 = unary, 2 = binary)
--   { tag = "KtProper" }                             — a fully-applied / structural
--       proper type (kind `*`): `Maybe Int`, a $record / $variant / $arrow / …
--   { tag = "KtVar", name = String }                 — a type variable: kind
--       unknown at the decl site ⇒ every predicate is conservative (False)
--   { tag = "KtUnknown" }                            — anything else
--
-- Phase 5c — the declared INPUT type `(t: KindType)` IS the marshal-selector
-- signal: the ByPattern seam (resolveStructural / universeStructuralInstancesFor)
-- reads each rule predicate's declared param-0 type from the function spec and
-- marshals the dispatched type via `marshalKindType` when it is `KindType` (these
-- predicates) vs `marshalTraversalType` for a structural predicate over
-- `TraversalType` (isRecordType). A Fenel-authored fact (the `.fenel` signature),
-- a registry spec read at the seam — NOT a TS hardcode of fn-ids
-- ([[feedback_no_language_concept_in_ts]]). KindType is an unregistered annotation
-- marker (like TraversalType — 0 entity decls), used only as the seam's classifier.
--
-- D-5a-2 — WRAPPER TRANSPARENCY = NOMINAL. The kind is the OUTER named
-- constructor's kind (Fenel dispatch is nominal); $opaque / $refined / $tagged
-- are reasoned through their named/pure view ($opaque is an optimization). A
-- bare `{$ref:"String"}` ⇒ KtCon "String" 0; the expanded $opaque ⇒ KtProper.
-- Both proper — consistent, no peeling.
--
-- Seam surprises heeded (the 3b-N idiom): no bare True/False in ARG position
-- (booleans live only in return position + the `if` guards); `eq` is SHALLOW —
-- every compare is on a pre-resolved String (the `tag`) or Number (the arity),
-- never a structural value.
-- =========================================================================


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- isProperType — kind `*`: a fully-saturated type. True for a nullary
-- constructor (declared arity 0 — Int / String) OR a fully-applied / structural
-- proper type (KtProper — Maybe Int, a $record, a $variant). A unary / binary
-- constructor (Maybe / Either) is NOT a proper type.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Is proper type"
@description "Well-kindedness predicate (kind `*`): True for a fully-saturated type — a nullary type constructor (declared arity 0, e.g. Int / String) or a fully-applied / structural proper type (KtProper — Maybe Int, a $record, a $variant, an $arrow). A unary / binary type constructor (Maybe / Either) is NOT proper. Reads the declared constructor arity surfaced on the marshalled KindType by marshalKindType (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts, category-B seam — the 3b-6 return-table precedent). Advisory; modelled on engine:isRecordType. unified-static-analysis Phase 5a."
@tags "engine" "kinds" "well-kindedness" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-5a"
isProperType : (t: KindType) -> Bool
isProperType t =
  if eq t.tag "KtCon" then eq t.arity 0
  else if eq t.tag "KtProper" then True
  else False


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- isUnaryConstructor — kind `* -> *`: a named type constructor of declared
-- arity EXACTLY 1. Maybe / List ⇒ True; Int / Either / an applied `Maybe Int`
-- ⇒ False. THE headline predicate — the Functor / Monad kind. `Functor Int`
-- rejects because Int (a nullary type, KtCon arity 0) is not a unary
-- constructor; `Functor (Maybe Int)` rejects because an applied type (KtProper)
-- is not a constructor at all.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Is unary constructor"
@description "Well-kindedness predicate (kind `* -> *`): True for a named type constructor of declared arity EXACTLY 1 (Maybe / List). Int (arity 0) / Either (arity 2) / an applied `Maybe Int` (KtProper) ⇒ False. The Functor / Monad class kind — checking `Functor f` is checking the `isUnaryConstructor f` predicate-bound. Reads the constructor arity surfaced on the marshalled KindType at the category-B kind-marshal seam. Advisory (the resolver wire is Phase 5b); modelled on engine:isRecordType. unified-static-analysis Phase 5a."
@tags "engine" "kinds" "well-kindedness" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-5a"
isUnaryConstructor : (t: KindType) -> Bool
isUnaryConstructor t = kindArityIs t 1


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- isBinaryConstructor — kind `* -> * -> *`: a named type constructor of
-- declared arity EXACTLY 2. Either / Result / Map ⇒ True. The Bifunctor /
-- Profunctor kind.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Is binary constructor"
@description "Well-kindedness predicate (kind `* -> * -> *`): True for a named type constructor of declared arity EXACTLY 2 (Either / Result / Map). The Bifunctor / Profunctor class kind. Reads the constructor arity surfaced on the marshalled KindType at the category-B kind-marshal seam. Advisory; modelled on engine:isRecordType. unified-static-analysis Phase 5a."
@tags "engine" "kinds" "well-kindedness" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-5a"
isBinaryConstructor : (t: KindType) -> Bool
isBinaryConstructor t = kindArityIs t 2


-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- kindArityIs — the shared core: True iff `t` is a named type constructor
-- (tag KtCon) whose declared arity equals `n`. The arity-comparison the two
-- constructor predicates are one-liners over (the isRecordType economy). A
-- KtProper / KtVar / KtUnknown is NOT a constructor of any arity ⇒ False. The
-- `t.arity` read is GUARDED behind the `eq t.tag "KtCon"` test, so a
-- non-KtCon marker (which carries no arity field) never touches it.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "kinds: arity is"
@description "Shared core for the constructor-arity predicates: True iff the marshalled KindType is a named constructor (tag KtCon) whose declared arity equals n. A proper / variable / unknown kind is not a constructor of any arity ⇒ False. The arity read is guarded behind the KtCon tag test. Internal helper; tagged engine-internal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "kinds" "unified-static-analysis" "phase-5a"
@category "engine-internal"
kindArityIs : (t: KindType) -> (n: Number) -> Bool
kindArityIs t n =
  if eq t.tag "KtCon" then eq t.arity n
  else False
